      "message": "Let an owner leave with everything, and let fsck survive a leaving\n\nNobody is kept. `cairn admin export --owner` writes what an owner leaves\nwith: a manifest of their repositories — name, default branch,\nvisibility, description, object format, archived — and a git bundle of\neach carrying every ref, so branches, tags, the change refs and the\nreceipt notes travel together and the receipts still verify against the\nforge they came from. Another forge takes them in through its operator:\nthe repository is made under the owner, and `import` with `everything`\nfetches every branch, recording each as imported history before\npublishing it, with the tags, notes and change refs as they are. A\n`file://` source is the operator's to give outside development, since\nit reads the box's own files; a bundle is handed to git as a path,\nbecause the url form would try to run upload-pack inside a file. A\ncompany on a forge of its own leaves with the nightly bundle, which is\nalready a forge.\n\nAnd fsck compared the live projections against a replay that had only\nthe projection tables, so the first deactivation on a forge — whose\narm ends the person's browser sessions, an operational table — made\nevery fsck after it fail with \"no such table\". The flagship found this\nthe day its first person was deactivated. The replay shadow now has\nthe whole schema; a test deactivates somebody and checks.\n\nChange-Id: Igraduation0110\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
